## 8. Spring Security affecting this endpoint

Two mutually-exclusive configs gated by property `petclinic.security.enable`:

- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/BasicAuthenticationConfig.java`** — active when `petclinic.security.enable=true`. `@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled = true)`, CSRF disabled, `anyRequest().authenticated()`, HTTP Basic. JDBC auth against `users`/`roles` tables, `BCryptPasswordEncoder`. Because method security is enabled, the controller's `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` is enforced — the caller must have role **`ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`** (`@roles` bean = `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/Roles.java`, `OWNER_ADMIN = "ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN"`).
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/DisableSecurityConfig.java`** — active when `petclinic.security.enable=false`. CSRF disabled, `anyRequest().permitAll()`, frame-options same-origin. Note: `@EnableMethodSecurity` is not present here, so `@PreAuthorize` is not enforced when security is disabled.
